    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d648">

                <pb facs="0678" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg668"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/7–549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hawthorne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-05T14:00:00+08:00">July 5, 1949—2 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:04 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>312. Director CUSA reports remaining ECA assets confiscated by Commies. These
                    include all cotton yarn due ECA from CTII<anchor n="49" xml:id="d648-f1"/> and
                    Hwahsing cotton mill, small stock flour and about 500 tons wheat, gunny bags and
                    flour sacks and 14,000 Chinese silver dollars CUSA had on hand for operating
                    expenses.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 312, repeated AmEmbOff Canton.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hawthorne</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d648-f1" n="49" xml:id="d648-f1-content">
                <p>China Textile Industries, Inc.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
